Why: cscc/ilrun shortcut (mono-2.6.4 basic profile compiled directly by 
pnet's cscc).  In Tokenizer.parse_less_than a case section ends with an 
inner switch whose every section, default included, ends in 'continue'.  
That is legal C#, but cscc's reachability analysis does not see that the 
inner switch cannot complete normally and reports "switch section falls 
through" (cs-tokenizer.cs:777).  Add an unreachable 'break;' for the 
BOOTSTRAP_WITH_OLDLIB (basic profile) build only.  New patch (not in Guix).

diff --git a/mcs/mcs/cs-tokenizer.cs b/mcs/mcs/cs-tokenizer.cs
index feff8405..0e24561c 100644
--- a/mcs/mcs/cs-tokenizer.cs
+++ b/mcs/mcs/cs-tokenizer.cs
@@ -773,6 +773,9 @@ namespace Mono.CSharp
 						can_be_type = is_type = false;
 						continue;
 					}
+#if BOOTSTRAP_WITH_OLDLIB
+					break;	// unreachable; cscc's flow analysis needs it
+#endif
 
 				case Token.OBJECT:
 				case Token.STRING:
